    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s May 14th slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Masyn Winn** (62.40) and **Will Smith** (61.79). **Masyn Winn** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Lopez, where a +10% park factor boost and favorable SP skill metrics propel him to our highest projected efficiency. **Will Smith** continues to be a staple; even with his lineup status technically pending, his projected #2 spot in the order provides an 8% boost that stabilizes his floor against Roupp. **Brendan Donovan** (61.16) also presents a strong play, leveraging a significant +14% platoon edge against Burrows, which comfortably offsets the minor park and SP skill penalties. These three remain our primary candidates for contributing to our counting categories today.\n\nThe middle of our lineup is currently navigating several soft spots, particularly regarding the Emmet Sheehan matchup. While **Luis Arraez** (47.91), **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.85), and **Matt Chapman** (43.49) are all active, they are fighting an uphill battle against Sheehan\u2019s elite xERA of 3.16, which triggered a heavy -19% SP skill penalty for all three. The most precarious decision of the day involves **Drew Gilbert** (37.35) sitting on the bench; he was the closest consideration for the final utility spot, but his assumed #8 spot in the order provided a -6% drag that ultimately pushed him below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" Similarly, **Bryson Stott** (45.09) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against the left-handed Ranger Suarez, though his score is propped up by a +7% park factor that keeps him just ahead of our bench alternatives. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, as four of our starters\u2014**Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman**\u2014are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" designations. If these projected batting orders fail to materialize, these scores could fluctuate significantly. We are intentionally holding **Wenceel Perez** (3